{"additions":255,"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa","databaseId":12109493}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #208\n\n### Changes\n- New `src/github/domain/viewer.rs`: `resolve(configured)` decides who \"me\" is, in this order\n  1. `github-login \"alice\"` from the config\n  2. `gh config get -h github.com user` — the account `gh auth login` stored in hosts.yml; a local lookup with no request, and it follows `gh auth switch`\n  3. the answer of an earlier `gh api user`, cached in `<cache>/vig/viewer.json` (`{ \"github.com\": \"td72\" }`; per host, not per repository)\n  4. `gh api user` as the last resort (saved into 3)\n- The Projects page's `assignee:@me` uses it; `gh api user` on every start is gone (`projects::client::viewer_login` removed)\n- Config node `github-login`: loader validation (one string, no whitespace, no leading `@`), merge allowlist, a comment in `default.kdl`\n- Fixtures: `config_get_-h_github.com_user.out` added; the recorder keeps both the `gh config get` and the `gh api user` answers\n- Tests: loader validation; a viewer replay test in its own process (`gh config get` before `gh api user`, an empty `user` entry is no answer)\n- Docs: a `github-login` section and table row in the Config Reference (en / ja), and a link from the `@me` note in the Projects chapter\n\n### Notes\n- The GitHub page does not use the login yet (#209 will)\n- No UI change, so no GIF was re-recorded\n- Only a `gh` signed in by token without a `user` entry ever reaches the API\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01GYXczwb9NyKFQNMJF7ukp2\n","changedFiles":13,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-04T05:50:07Z","deletions":21,"headRefName":"feat/viewer-login","isDraft":false,"labels":[],"number":211,"reviewDecision":"","reviewRequests":[],"reviews":[],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__ty